om><a:noFill/><a:ln/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" lIns="0" tIns="0" rIns="0" bIns="0" rtlCol="0" anchor="t"/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPts val="1250"/></a:lnSpc><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="1A1A1A"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>A discussion is required on how approval for the bridge is to be secured, and in particular whether a revised physical model must be submitted to the IRC or whether the January 2023 model may stand, the numerical modelling being promising. The question is one of technical acceptance rather than of legal requirement, and any reliance on the earlier model must be reconciled with the change in the design premise recorded at item 1.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1000" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>